{"id":"mahabharata-2-011","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":11,"title":"एकादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 11 · The hall of Brahma and Pandu's message","summary":{"en":"Narada describes Brahma's indescribable hall, where all the gods, sages and powers attend the creator. Asked why only Harishchandra among kings reached Indra's hall, he explains it was by the royal consecration sacrifice, and he brings a message from Pandu urging Yudhishthira to perform it.","kn":"ಎಲ್ಲ ದೇವತೆಗಳೂ ಋಷಿಗಳೂ ಶಕ್ತಿಗಳೂ ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಕರ್ತನನ್ನು ಸೇವಿಸುವ ಅವರ್ಣನೀಯ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಸಭೆಯನ್ನು ನಾರದರು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ರಾಜರಲ್ಲಿ ಹರಿಶ್ಚಂದ್ರನೊಬ್ಬನೇ ಇಂದ್ರಸಭೆ ಸೇರಿದ್ದು ರಾಜಸೂಯದಿಂದ ಎಂದು ವಿವರಿಸಿ, ಅದನ್ನು ಮಾಡೆಂದು ಪಾಂಡುವಿನ ಸಂದೇಶವನ್ನು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"नारद ब्रह्मा की अवर्णनीय सभा का वर्णन करते हैं, जहाँ सब देवता, ऋषि और शक्तियाँ स्रष्टा की सेवा करते हैं। यह पूछे जाने पर कि राजाओं में केवल हरिश्चन्द्र ही इन्द्र की सभा में क्यों पहुँचे, वे बताते हैं कि राजसूय यज्ञ के कारण, और पाण्डु का सन्देश देते हैं कि युधिष्ठिर उसे करें।","te":"అన్ని దేవతలు, ఋషులు, శక్తులు సృష్టికర్తను సేవించే వర్ణనాతీతమైన బ్రహ్మసభను నారదుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు. రాజులలో హరిశ్చంద్రుడొక్కడే ఇంద్రసభ చేరడానికి కారణం రాజసూయమని వివరించి, దానిని చేయమని పాండురాజు సందేశాన్ని యుధిష్ఠిరునికి అందిస్తాడు.","ta":"எல்லாத் தேவர்களும் முனிவர்களும் ஆற்றல்களும் படைப்பாளரைச் சேவிக்கும் சொல்லொணா ப்ரஹ்ம ஸபையை நாரதர் வர்ணிக்கிறார். மன்னர்களில் ஹரிஶ்சந்திரன் ஒருவனே இந்திர ஸபையை அடைந்தது ராஜஸூய யாகத்தால் என்று விளக்கி, அதைச் செய்யுமாறு பாண்டுவின் செய்தியை யுதிஷ்டிரருக்குச் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"വിവരിക്കാനാവാത്ത ബ്രഹ്മാവിന്റെ സഭയെ നാരദൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; സ്രഷ്ടാവിനെ എല്ലാ ദേവന്മാരും ഋഷിമാരും ശക്തികളും സേവിക്കുന്നു. രാജാക്കന്മാരിൽ ഹരിശ്ചന്ദ്രൻ മാത്രം ഇന്ദ്രസഭയിൽ എത്തിയതെന്തുകൊണ്ടെന്ന് ചോദിക്കപ്പെട്ട അദ്ദേഹം, അത് രാജസൂയ യജ്ഞത്താലായിരുന്നുവെന്ന് വിശദീകരിക്കുന്നു; അത് നടത്താൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനോട് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്ന പാണ്ഡുവിന്റെ സന്ദേശവും അദ്ദേഹം കൊണ്ടുവരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.11; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"सभापर्व","titleEn":"Sabha Parva (The assembly hall)","verses":[{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पुरा देवयुगे राजन्नादित्यो भगवान्दिवः ।\nआगच्छन्मानुषं लोकं दिदृक्षुर्विगतक्लमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the age of the gods long ago, O king, the blessed sun, free of weariness, came down from heaven to the world of men, wishing to see it."}},{"n":2,"text":"चरन्मानुषरूपेण सभां दृष्ट्वा स्वयंभुवः ।\nसभामकथयन्मह्यं ब्राह्मीं तत्त्वेन पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Walking in human form, he had seen the hall of the Self-born, and he described to me truly that hall of Brahma, O Pandava."}},{"n":3,"text":"अप्रमेयप्रभां दिव्यां मानसीं भरतर्षभ ।\nअनिर्देश्यां प्रभावेन सर्वभूतमनोरमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is of immeasurable radiance, heavenly, made by the mind, O bull of the Bharatas, beyond description in its power, and delightful to the minds of all beings."}},{"n":4,"text":"श्रुत्वा गुणानहं तस्याः सभायाः पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nदर्शनेप्सुस्तथा राजन्नादित्यमहमब्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing of the merits of that hall, son of Pandu, I longed to see it, and I said to the Sun,"}},{"n":5,"text":"भगवन्द्रष्टुमिच्छामि पितामहसभामहम् ।\nयेन सा तपसा शक्या कर्मणा वापि गोपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Blessed one, I wish to see the grandfather's hall. By what austerity or work could it be reached, lord of rays,"}},{"n":6,"text":"औषधैर्वा तथा युक्तैरुत वा मायया यया ।\nतन्ममाचक्ष्व भगवन्पश्येयं तां सभां कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"or by what proper remedies, or by what magic? Tell me, blessed one, how I might see that hall.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः स भगवान्सूर्यो मामुपादाय वीर्यवान् ।\nअगच्छत्तां सभां ब्राह्मीं विपापां विगतक्लमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty, blessed Sun took me with him and went to that hall of Brahma, free of sin and of weariness."}},{"n":8,"text":"एवंरूपेति सा शक्या न निर्देष्टुं जनाधिप ।\nक्षणेन हि बिभर्त्यन्यदनिर्देश्यं वपुस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It cannot be pointed out as \"of such a form,\" O lord of the people; for in an instant it takes another form that likewise cannot be described."}},{"n":9,"text":"न वेद परिमाणं वा संस्थानं वापि भारत ।\nन च रूपं मया तादृग्दृष्टपूर्वं कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not know its measure or its plan, Bharata, nor had I ever seen such a form before."}},{"n":10,"text":"सुसुखा सा सभा राजन्न शीता न च घर्मदा ।\nन क्षुत्पिपासे न ग्लानिं प्राप्य तां प्राप्नुवन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hall is most pleasant, O king, neither cold nor hot; hunger, thirst and weariness do not touch those who reach it."}},{"n":11,"text":"नानारूपैरिव कृता सुविचित्रैः सुभास्वरैः ।\nस्तम्भैर्न च धृता सा तु शाश्वती न च सा क्षरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It seems built of many varied, brilliant forms, yet no pillars hold it; it is everlasting and never decays."}},{"n":12,"text":"अति चन्द्रं च सूर्यं च शिखिनं च स्वयंप्रभा ।\nदीप्यते नाकपृष्ठस्था भासयन्तीव भास्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It shines by its own light, outshining the moon, the sun and fire, standing on the back of the sky as if it lit up the sun itself."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्यां स भगवानास्ते विदधद्देवमायया ।\nस्वयमेकोऽनिशं राजँल्लोकाँल्लोकपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In it the blessed one, the grandfather of the worlds, sits, creating the worlds alone by divine power, O king, without pause."}},{"n":14,"text":"उपतिष्ठन्ति चाप्येनं प्रजानां पतयः प्रभुम् ।\nदक्षः प्रचेताः पुलहो मरीचिः कश्यपस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lords of creatures attend that lord there: Daksha, Prachetas, Pulaha, Marichi and Kashyapa;"}},{"n":15,"text":"भृगुरत्रिर्वसिष्ठश्च गौतमश्च तथाङ्गिराः ।\nमनोऽन्तरिक्षं विद्याश्च वायुस्तेजो जलं मही ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhrigu, Atri, Vasishtha, Gautama and Angiras; Mind, space, the sciences, wind, fire, water and earth;"}},{"n":16,"text":"शब्दः स्पर्शस्तथा रूपं रसो गन्धश्च भारत ।\nप्रकृतिश्च विकारश्च यच्चान्यत्कारणं भुवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"sound, touch, form, taste and smell, O Bharata; nature and its changes, and whatever else is a cause of the world."}},{"n":17,"text":"चन्द्रमाः सह नक्षत्रैरादित्यश्च गभस्तिमान् ।\nवायवः क्रतवश्चैव संकल्पः प्राण एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The moon with the stars, and the radiant sun; the winds and sacrifices; resolve and breath."}},{"n":18,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवः स्वयंभुवमुपस्थिताः ।\nअर्थो धर्मश्च कामश्च हर्षो द्वेषस्तपो दमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and many others stand before the Self-born, as do wealth, dharma and desire, joy and hatred, austerity and self-control."}},{"n":19,"text":"आयान्ति तस्यां सहिता गन्धर्वाप्सरसस्तथा ।\nविंशतिः सप्त चैवान्ये लोकपालाश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gandharvas and Apsarases come there together, and twenty-seven others, and all the guardians of the worlds."}},{"n":20,"text":"शुक्रो बृहस्पतिश्चैव बुधोऽङ्गारक एव च ।\nशनैश्चरश्च राहुश्च ग्रहाः सर्वे तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shukra, Brihaspati, Budha, Angaraka, Shanaishchara and Rahu, all the planets are there too."}},{"n":21,"text":"मन्त्रो रथंतरश्चैव हरिमान्वसुमानपि ।\nआदित्याः साधिराजानो नानाद्वंद्वैरुदाहृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mantra, the Rathantara chant, Harimat and Vasumat, the Adityas with their chief, named in many pairs,"}},{"n":22,"text":"मरुतो विश्वकर्मा च वसवश्चैव भारत ।\nतथा पितृगणाः सर्वे सर्वाणि च हवींष्यथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Maruts, Vishvakarma, the Vasus, O Bharata, all the groups of fathers, and all the oblations."}},{"n":23,"text":"ऋग्वेदः सामवेदश्च यजुर्वेदश्च पाण्डव ।\nअथर्ववेदश्च तथा पर्वाणि च विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Rigveda, Samaveda, Yajurveda and Atharvaveda, Pandava, and the sacred junctures of the months, O lord of the people;"}},{"n":24,"text":"इतिहासोपवेदाश्च वेदाङ्गानि च सर्वशः ।\nग्रहा यज्ञाश्च सोमश्च दैवतानि च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Itihasa and the Upavedas, all the limbs of the Vedas, the planets, the sacrifices, Soma and all the deities;"}},{"n":25,"text":"सावित्री दुर्गतरणी वाणी सप्तविधा तथा ।\nमेधा धृतिः श्रुतिश्चैव प्रज्ञा बुद्धिर्यशः क्षमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Savitri, the one who carries across hard places, the sevenfold Speech, Insight, Steadfastness, Revelation, Wisdom, Understanding, Fame and Patience;"}},{"n":26,"text":"सामानि स्तुतिशस्त्राणि गाथाश्च विविधास्तथा ।\nभाष्याणि तर्कयुक्तानि देहवन्ति विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Samans, hymns and recitations, the many ballads, and commentaries with their reasoning, in bodily form, O lord of the people."}},{"n":27,"text":"क्षणा लवा मुहूर्ताश्च दिवा रात्रिस्तथैव च ।\nअर्धमासाश्च मासाश्च ऋतवः षट्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The moments, instants and hours, day and night, half-months and months, and the six seasons, O Bharata;"}},{"n":28,"text":"संवत्सराः पञ्चयुगमहोरात्राश्चतुर्विधाः ।\nकालचक्रं च यद्दिव्यं नित्यमक्षयमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the years, the five-year cycle, the four kinds of days and nights, and the heavenly wheel of time, ever undecaying and unchanging."}},{"n":29,"text":"अदितिर्दितिर्दनुश्चैव सुरसा विनता इरा ।\nकालका सुरभिर्देवी सरमा चाथ गौतमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aditi, Diti, Danu, Surasa, Vinata, Ira, Kalaka, the goddess Surabhi, Sarama and Gautami;"}},{"n":30,"text":"आदित्या वसवो रुद्रा मरुतश्चाश्विनावपि ।\nविश्वेदेवाश्च साध्याश्च पितरश्च मनोजवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Adityas, Vasus, Rudras, Maruts and the Ashvins, the Vishvedevas, Sadhyas, and the fathers swift as thought;"}},{"n":31,"text":"राक्षसाश्च पिशाचाश्च दानवा गुह्यकास्तथा ।\nसुपर्णनागपशवः पितामहमुपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rakshasas, Pishachas, Danavas, Guhyakas, the Suparnas, nagas and beasts attend the grandfather."}},{"n":32,"text":"देवो नारायणस्तस्यां तथा देवर्षयश्च ये ।\nऋषयो वालखिल्याश्च योनिजायोनिजास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The god Narayana is there, and the divine seers, the seers, the Valakhilyas, those born of the womb and those not."}},{"n":33,"text":"यच्च किंचित्त्रिलोकेऽस्मिन्दृश्यते स्थाणुजङ्गमम् ।\nसर्वं तस्यां मया दृष्टं तद्विद्धि मनुजाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever is seen in these three worlds, moving or still, all of it I saw there; know this, O lord of men."}},{"n":34,"text":"अष्टाशीतिसहस्राणि यतीनामूर्ध्वरेतसाम् ।\nप्रजावतां च पञ्चाशदृषीणामपि पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eighty-eight thousand ascetics of upward-flowing seed, and fifty seers who have children, Pandava,"}},{"n":35,"text":"ते स्म तत्र यथाकामं दृष्ट्वा सर्वे दिवौकसः ।\nप्रणम्य शिरसा तस्मै प्रतियान्ति यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"having seen all those who dwell in heaven there, as they wished, bow their heads to him and go back as they came."}},{"n":36,"text":"अतिथीनागतान्देवान्दैत्यान्नागान्मुनींस्तथा ।\nयक्षान्सुपर्णान्कालेयान्गन्धर्वाप्सरसस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma, the grandfather of the worlds, of boundless understanding and compassionate to all beings, receives them fittingly: the gods who come as guests, the Daityas, nagas, sages,"}},{"n":37,"text":"महाभागानमितधीर्ब्रह्मा लोकपितामहः ।\nदयावान्सर्वभूतेषु यथार्हं प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yakshas, Suparnas, Kaleyas, Gandharvas and Apsarases, all of great fortune."}},{"n":38,"text":"प्रतिगृह्य च विश्वात्मा स्वयंभूरमितप्रभः ।\nसान्त्वमानार्थसंभोगैर्युनक्ति मनुजाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Self of all, the self-born, of boundless radiance, receives them and gratifies them with kind words, honor and enjoyments, O lord of men."}},{"n":39,"text":"तथा तैरुपयातैश्च प्रतियातैश्च भारत ।\nआकुला सा सभा तात भवति स्म सुखप्रदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With those arriving and those departing, that hall, my dear, is crowded and yet gives happiness, O Bharata."}},{"n":40,"text":"सर्वतेजोमयी दिव्या ब्रह्मर्षिगणसेविता ।\nब्राह्म्या श्रिया दीप्यमाना शुशुभे विगतक्लमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heavenly, made wholly of splendor and served by troops of Brahmin seers, it shone, blazing with Brahma's glory, free of weariness."}},{"n":41,"text":"सा सभा तादृशी दृष्टा सर्वलोकेषु दुर्लभा ।\nसभेयं राजशार्दूल मनुष्येषु यथा तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such a hall I saw, one hard to find in any world; this hall of yours, tiger among kings, is the like of it among men."}},{"n":42,"text":"एता मया दृष्टपूर्वाः सभा देवेषु पाण्डव ।\nतवेयं मानुषे लोके सर्वश्रेष्ठतमा सभा ॥","meaning":{"en":"These halls I have seen before among the gods, Pandava; yours in the world of men is the best of all."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"प्रायशो राजलोकस्ते कथितो वदतां वर ।\nवैवस्वतसभायां तु यथा वदसि वै प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of speakers, you have mostly told me about the halls of kings in the world of Vaivasvata's hall, as you say, lord."}},{"n":44,"text":"वरुणस्य सभायां तु नागास्ते कथिता विभो ।\nदैत्येन्द्राश्चैव भूयिष्ठाः सरितः सागरास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In Varuna's hall, great one, you spoke of nagas, chiefly of the lords of the Daityas, and of rivers and seas."}},{"n":45,"text":"तथा धनपतेर्यक्षा गुह्यका राक्षसास्तथा ।\nगन्धर्वाप्सरसश्चैव भगवांश्च वृषध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In Kubera's hall, of Yakshas, Guhyakas and Rakshasas, of Gandharvas and Apsarases, and of the blessed one with the bull banner."}},{"n":46,"text":"पितामहसभायां तु कथितास्ते महर्षयः ।\nसर्वदेवनिकायाश्च सर्वशास्त्राणि चैव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the grandfather's hall you named the great seers, all the orders of the gods and all the sciences."}},{"n":47,"text":"शतक्रतुसभायां तु देवाः संकीर्तिता मुने ।\nउद्देशतश्च गन्धर्वा विविधाश्च महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the hall of Shatakratu, sage, you mentioned the gods, and in outline the Gandharvas and the various great seers."}},{"n":48,"text":"एक एव तु राजर्षिर्हरिश्चन्द्रो महामुने ।\nकथितस्ते सभानित्यो देवेन्द्रस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But of royal seers, great sage, only Harishchandra was named by you, always sitting in the hall of the great lord of the gods."}},{"n":49,"text":"किं कर्म तेनाचरितं तपो वा नियतव्रतम् ।\nयेनासौ सह शक्रेण स्पर्धते स्म महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What deed did he do, or what austerity of fixed vows, that this man of great fame rivaled Shakra?"}},{"n":50,"text":"पितृलोकगतश्चापि त्वया विप्र पिता मम ।\nदृष्टः पाण्डुर्महाभागः कथं चासि समागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And, Brahmin, you saw my father Pandu, of great fortune, when you went to the world of the fathers; how did you come to meet him?"}},{"n":51,"text":"किमुक्तवांश्च भगवन्नेतदिच्छामि वेदितुम् ।\nत्वत्तः श्रोतुमहं सर्वं परं कौतूहलं हि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"What did he say, blessed one? This I wish to know; I want to hear all of it from you, for my curiosity is very great."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":52,"text":"यन्मां पृच्छसि राजेन्द्र हरिश्चन्द्रं प्रति प्रभो ।\nतत्तेऽहं संप्रवक्ष्यामि माहात्म्यं तस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What you ask me, king of kings, about Harishchandra, I will tell you, the greatness of that wise man."}},{"n":53,"text":"स राजा बलवानासीत्सम्राट्सर्वमहीक्षिताम् ।\nतस्य सर्वे महीपालाः शासनावनताः स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king was mighty, emperor over all the earth's rulers; all the lords of the earth stood bowing to his command."}},{"n":54,"text":"तेनैकं रथमास्थाय जैत्रं हेमविभूषितम् ।\nशस्त्रप्रतापेन जिता द्वीपाः सप्त नरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting a single victorious chariot adorned with gold, he conquered the seven continents by the might of his weapons, O lord of men."}},{"n":55,"text":"स विजित्य महीं सर्वां सशैलवनकाननाम् ।\nआजहार महाराज राजसूयं महाक्रतुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having conquered the whole earth with its mountains, forests and groves, great king, he performed the great sacrifice, the Rajasuya."}},{"n":56,"text":"तस्य सर्वे महीपाला धनान्याजह्रुराज्ञया ।\nद्विजानां परिवेष्टारस्तस्मिन्यज्ञे च तेऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his command all the kings brought him wealth, and at that sacrifice they served the Brahmins as attendants."}},{"n":57,"text":"प्रादाच्च द्रविणं प्रीत्या याजकानां नरेश्वरः ।\nयथोक्तं तत्र तैस्तस्मिंस्ततः पञ्चगुणाधिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That lord of men gladly gave the sacrificial priests there wealth, five times more than what had been promised."}},{"n":58,"text":"अतर्पयच्च विविधैर्वसुभिर्ब्राह्मणांस्तथा ।\nप्रासर्पकाले संप्राप्ते नानादिग्भ्यः समागतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the time for the closing rites came, he satisfied the Brahmins who had come from many directions with riches of many kinds,"}},{"n":59,"text":"भक्ष्यैर्भोज्यैश्च विविधैर्यथाकामपुरस्कृतैः ।\nरत्नौघतर्पितैस्तुष्टैर्द्विजैश्च समुदाहृतम् ।\nतेजस्वी च यशस्वी च नृपेभ्योऽभ्यधिकोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and with foods and dishes of many kinds, offered as they wished; the Brahmins, pleased and gratified by heaps of jewels, spoke in his praise. He became more brilliant and more famous than all other kings."}},{"n":60,"text":"एतस्मात्कारणात्पार्थ हरिश्चन्द्रो विराजते ।\nतेभ्यो राजसहस्रेभ्यस्तद्विद्धि भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this reason, Partha, Harishchandra shines above those thousands of kings; know this, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":61,"text":"समाप्य च हरिश्चन्द्रो महायज्ञं प्रतापवान् ।\nअभिषिक्तः स शुशुभे साम्राज्येन नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the mighty Harishchandra had finished the great sacrifice, he was consecrated and shone with imperial rule, O lord of men."}},{"n":62,"text":"ये चान्येऽपि महीपाला राजसूयं महाक्रतुम् ।\nयजन्ते ते महेन्द्रेण मोदन्ते सह भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other kings too who perform the great Rajasuya sacrifice rejoice with the great Indra, O Bharata."}},{"n":63,"text":"ये चापि निधनं प्राप्ताः संग्रामेष्वपलायिनः ।\nते तत्सदः समासाद्य मोदन्ते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those who die in battle without turning back, O bull of the Bharatas, reach that hall and rejoice there."}},{"n":64,"text":"तपसा ये च तीव्रेण त्यजन्तीह कलेवरम् ।\nतेऽपि तत्स्थानमासाद्य श्रीमन्तो भान्ति नित्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who give up the body here by fierce austerity also reach that place and shine there always in splendor."}},{"n":65,"text":"पिता च त्वाह कौन्तेय पाण्डुः कौरवनन्दनः ।\nहरिश्चन्द्रे श्रियं दृष्ट्वा नृपतौ जातविस्मयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father Pandu, delight of the Kurus, said to you, Kaunteya, struck with wonder on seeing Harishchandra's fortune:"}},{"n":66,"text":"समर्थोऽसि महीं जेतुं भ्रातरस्ते वशे स्थिताः ।\nराजसूयं क्रतुश्रेष्ठमाहरस्वेति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are able to conquer the earth, your brothers are under your sway; perform the Rajasuya, best of sacrifices, Bharata.\""}},{"n":67,"text":"तस्य त्वं पुरुषव्याघ्र संकल्पं कुरु पाण्डव ।\nगन्तारस्ते महेन्द्रस्य पूर्वैः सह सलोकताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Make the resolve to do it, tiger among men, Pandava, and you will go to Mahendra's world together with your forefathers.\""}},{"n":68,"text":"बहुविघ्नश्च नृपते क्रतुरेष स्मृतो महान् ।\nछिद्राण्यत्र हि वाञ्छन्ति यज्ञघ्ना ब्रह्मराक्षसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great sacrifice is said to have many obstacles, O king, for the Brahmin demons who destroy sacrifices look for flaws in it."}},{"n":69,"text":"युद्धं च पृष्ठगमनं पृथिवीक्षयकारकम् ।\nकिंचिदेव निमित्तं च भवत्यत्र क्षयावहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"War, retreat and the ruin of the earth may arise, and some small cause here can bring destruction."}},{"n":70,"text":"एतत्संचिन्त्य राजेन्द्र यत्क्षमं तत्समाचर ।\nअप्रमत्तोत्थितो नित्यं चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य रक्षणे ।\nभव एधस्व मोदस्व दानैस्तर्पय च द्विजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Considering this, king of kings, do what is fitting; always alert and ready to protect the four classes, rule, prosper and rejoice, and satisfy the Brahmins with gifts."}},{"n":71,"text":"एतत्ते विस्तरेणोक्तं यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ।\nआपृच्छे त्वां गमिष्यामि दाशार्हनगरीं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"All that you asked me I have told at length; I take my leave of you, for I will go to the city of the Dasharhas."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":72,"text":"एवमाख्याय पार्थेभ्यो नारदो जनमेजय ।\nजगाम तैर्वृतो राजन्नृषिभिर्यैः समागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having told the Pandavas all this, Narada, O Janamejaya, went away, surrounded by the sages with whom he had come."}},{"n":73,"text":"गते तु नारदे पार्थो भ्रातृभिः सह कौरव ।\nराजसूयं क्रतुश्रेष्ठं चिन्तयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Narada had gone, Partha, with his brothers, O Kaurava, thought about the Rajasuya, the best of sacrifices."}}]}]}